# AmentCase Desktop

The Windows companion app for **AmentCase**, the practice-management
system used at Ament Law Group, P.C.

This repository is the official **download and auto-update home** for the
desktop app. The application's source code is maintained privately; only
the published installers are distributed here so the app can check for
and download updates.

## Download & install

1. Open the [**latest release**](../../releases/latest).
2. Download **`AmentCaseDesktop-Setup.exe`**.
3. Run it. The installer is per-user and needs no administrator rights.
4. Sign in with your AmentCase credentials on first launch.

The installer is digitally signed by **Ament Law Group, PC**. To check a
download before running it, right-click the file, choose **Properties**,
and open the **Digital Signatures** tab: the signer should be
"Ament Law Group, PC". If that tab is missing or names anyone else, do not
run the file; tell the firm's IT/admin channel.

Windows may still show a SmartScreen prompt for a newly published
release. The prompt names the publisher. Continue only when it reads
**Ament Law Group, PC**.

## What the app does

- **Passive time tracking** — quietly records time against the matter
  you're working in, so billable work isn't lost.
- **AmentCase (V:) drive** — mounts your matter documents as a Windows
  drive. Open and edit files in Word; saves go straight back to the
  matter vault as new versions.
- **One-click integrations** — sets up the Word add-in and document
  workflows for your account.
- **Quick actions** — log calls, scan, dictate, and file documents from
  the tray.

## Automatic updates

The app checks this repository for new releases and notifies you when an
update is available. You can also check any time from the tray menu →
**Check for updates…**. Installing a newer release over an existing one
preserves your settings. Before it runs a downloaded update, the app
checks that the installer is signed by Ament Law Group, PC.

## Versioning

Releases are tagged `vYYYY.MM.DD.NN` (the date published, then a two-digit
counter for the releases cut that day). Some older releases were tagged
in other orders; the app reads all of them and only installs a release
newer than the one it is running. The tray menu and **Apps & features**
both show the installed version.

## Support

Staff: contact the firm's IT/admin channel for help, or email
**support@amentcase.com**.

